    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP\u2019s July 21st slate, our offensive ceiling is anchored by **James Wood** (78.42), who earns the top spot in the lineup against Lorenzen. With an elite 0.428 xwOBA and a generous 14% park boost, **James Wood** is perfectly positioned to leverage his #1 lineup spot. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (73.15) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) offer excellent utility; **Vinnie Pasquantino** in particular enjoys a massive 14% platoon edge against Mahle, while **Isaac Paredes** benefits from facing a favorable 4.81 xERA matchup. We are also leaning heavily on the upside of **Corbin Carroll** (64.55) and **Austin Riley** (66.86), the latter of whom gains significant momentum from a favorable wind direction (Out) and a solid SP matchup against Buehler.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved keeping **Josh Naylor** (53.14) on the bench. While his projection remained competitive, the combination of a tough outing against Burns and a park penalty suppressed his efficiency score just enough to keep him behind the primary starters. We opted to prioritize the platoon-heavy profiles of **Max Muncy** and **Tyler Soderstrom** against Drake, whose profile allows our bats to exploit his L/L splits. We are monitoring the weather in **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s contest closely; despite a strong 62.00 score and favorable SP delivery mechanics for stealing bases, the 42% rain risk is a notable volatility flag that could shorten his playing time. Additionally, keep an eye on **Brice Turang**; despite his high floor, his SB potential is hampered slightly by a tough catcher matchup, though he remains a key piece in our pursuit of category scarcity.",
